{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he told his father and his brothers.</b> After he told it to his brothers, he went back and told it to his father in their presence." "<b>And he rebuked him.</b> Because he was casting hatred upon him." "<b>Will we come, indeed.</b> But is your mother not already dead? And he did not know that the matter extends to Bilhah, who raised him as his mother. And our Sages learned from here that no dream is without idle elements, and Jacob intended to remove the matter from the hearts of his sons so that they would not be envious of him — therefore he said to him, הֲבוֹא נָבוֹא etc. — just as it is impossible with your mother, so too the rest is idle."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:23.207133225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}